{
  "id": "Compound::DB00578 - Gene::9356",
  "verbalization": "Carbenicillin, a member of the penicillin class of antibiotics, is linked to Slc22a6 through a shared biological pathway involving beta-lactam antibiotics. The evidence suggests that Carbenicillin, through its inclusion in the penicillin family, binds to Slc22a6, which is a transporter protein involved in the uptake of various substrates. This relationship is reinforced by the presence of multiple lowest common ancestors, indicating that Carbenicillin is functionally related to Nafcillin, a closely related beta-lactam antibiotic, which itself binds to Slc22a6. The overlapping pathways and the shared biological role of Slc22a6 in transporting substrates suggest a mechanism where Carbenicillin, as part of the penicillin class, influences Slc22a6 through its structural and functional similarities to other beta-lactam antibiotics. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which Carbenicillin may interact with Slc22a6, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
